.TITLE "node"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
An open-source, cross-platform JavaScript runtime environment that executes code outside a web browser. It is built on Chrome's __V8 engine__ and is primarily used for building scalable __network applications__.

.DIV "TLDR"
**node file.js**
Executes a specific JavaScript file.
> __file.js__ the script to run

**node -v**
Displays the current version of the installed environment.
> __-v__ version flag

**node -e "code"**
Evaluates and runs a string of JavaScript code directly from the terminal.
> __-e__ eval flag | __"code"__ the javascript string

**node --watch file.js**
Starts a process that restarts automatically when the file changes.
> __--watch__ restart on change flag | __file.js__ target script

**node --check file.js**
Checks the syntax of a script without executing it.
> __--check__ syntax check flag | __file.js__ target script

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using the __--watch__ flag during development significantly improves productivity by removing the need to manually restart the process. Always ensure your __node modules__ are up to date to avoid runtime compatibility issues.

